REGENT OF MUNA SOUTHEAST SULAWESI PROVINCE REGIONAL REGULATION OF MUNA REGENCY NUMBER 7 OF 2019

REGENT OF MUNA SOUTHEAST SULAWESI PROVINCE REGIONAL REGULATION OF MUNA REGENCY NUMBER 7 OF 2019

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE IN MUNA REGENCY

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF MUNA.

Considering : a. that discrimination and violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights and crimes against humanity;

b. that in order to fulfill the constitutional rights of women and children and improve the quality of life, it is necessary to regulate the duties, authorities and responsibilities of the Regional Government in the protection of women and children victims of violence;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is deemed necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence in Muna Regency.

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia; 2. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277); 3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886); 4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State

Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as has been amended several times most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 Concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

6. Law Number 13 of 2006 Concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia number 4635) as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 Concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia number 5602);

7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);

8. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning the Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5234);

9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been most recently amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5659);

10. Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);

11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation in the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

13. Regulation of the State Minister for Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning

Guidelines for the Empowerment of Children Victims of Violence. 14. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Legal Products, as has been amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 120 of 2018 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formulation of Regional Regulations;

With the Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL OF MUNA REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF MUNA

DECIDES:

To enact :REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE IN MUNA REGENCY CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

text:
Pasal 3

(1)Tujuan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan, adalah untuk: a. mencegah tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak termasuk perdagangan orang; b. menghapus segala bentuk kekerasan dan eksploitasi terhadap perempuan dan anak; c. melindungi dan memberikan rasa aman bagi perempuan dan anak; d. memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan, pelapor dan saksi; e. memfasilitasi dan melakukan mediasi terhadap sengketa rumah tangga untuk mewujudkan keutuhan rumah tangga yang harmonis dan sejahtera.

(2) Kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa:

a. kekerasan fisik;
b. kekerasan psikis;
c. kekerasan seksual;
d. penelantaran ekonomi;
e. pembatasan ruang gerak.

translated_text:
Article 3

(1)The purpose of protecting women and children victims of violence, is to: a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including human trafficking; b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children; c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; d. provide services to women and children victims of violence, reporters and witnesses; e. facilitate and mediate domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

(2) Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of:

a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic neglect;
e. restriction of movement.

text:
BAB III HAK-HAK KORBAN

Pasal 4

Setiap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan berhak untuk mendapatkan:

a. untuk dihormati harkat dan martabatnya sebagai manusia;
b. perlindungan dari pihak keluarga, masyarakat, pemerintah daerah dan/atau pihak lain baik sementara maupun berdasarkan penetapan pemerintah, perlindungan dari pengadilan;
c. pelayanan kesehatan sesuai kebutuhan medis;
d. penanganan secara khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan korban;
e. pendampingan oleh pekerja sosial dan bantuan hukum pada setiap tingkat proses pemeriksaan sesuai dengan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang- undangan;
f. pelayanan bimbingan rohani;
g. menentukan sendiri keputusannya;

translated_text:
CHAPTER III RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 4

Every woman and child victim of violence has the right to receive:

a. respect for their dignity and worth as human beings;
b. protection from family, community, regional government and/or other parties either temporarily or based on government determination, protection from the court;
c. health services according to medical needs;
d. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
e. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
f. spiritual guidance services;
g. determine their own decisions;

text:
BAB IV KEWAJIBAN DAN TANGGUNGJAWAB

Pasal 5

Kewajiban dan tanggungjawab dalam memberikan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan merupakan tanggungjawab bersama:

a. pemerintah daerah dan pemerintah desa;
b. masyarakat;
c. keluarga;
d. orang tua.

translated_text:
CHAPTER IV OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

Article 5

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children victims of violence are the shared responsibility of:

a. regional government and village government;
b. community;
c. family;
d. parents.

text:
Pasal 6

(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggungjawab dalam memberikan perlindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.

(2) Kewajiban dan tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf a meliputi:

a. melaksanakan kebijakan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan berdasarkan Peraturan Perundang-undangan;
b. menetapkan kebijakan, program dan kegiatan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
c. memberikan dukungan sarana dan prasarana pelaksanaan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
d. memfasilitasi pendampingan, bantuan hukum dan pelayanan hukum sesuai kebutuhan korban;
e. mengalokasikan anggaran penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari korban kekerasan sesuai kemampuan keuangan daerah; dan
f. membina dan mengawasasi penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan.
(3) Kewajiban Pemerintah Desa sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf a meliputi:
a. menetapkan kebijakan untuk perlindungan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan, seperti Peraturan Desa tentang Perlindungan Perempuan dan Anak atau Peraturan Kepala Desa;
b. memasukan program perlindungan perempuan dan anak dalam Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Desa;
c. mengalokasikan anggaran untuk kegiatan penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dalam Anggaran Pendapatan dan Belanja Desa;
d. membentuk posko desa untuk pelayanan terpadu bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
e. menyediakan program layanan bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan di desa;
f. mengangkat pengurus dan petugas pendamping korban untuk posko desa;
g. melakukan kegiatan pencegahan di desa;
h. melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama dengan pihak terkait termasuk dengan masyarakat, layanan berbasis komunitas dan dunia usaha;
i. melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak di tingkat desa.
(4) Dalam rangka melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggungjawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Bupati menetapkan program dan kegiatan aksi perlindungan perempuan dan anak dalam satu rencana aksi daerah sebagai dasar bagi OPD dalam melaksanakan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(5) Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (4) merupakan bagian dari Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Daerah (RPJMD).

translated_text:
Article 6

(1) The Regional Government is obligated and responsible for providing protection to women and children victims of violence.

(2) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 5 letter a include:

a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children victims of violence based on Laws and Regulations;
b. establishing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women and children victims of violence;
c. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence;
d. facilitating assistance, legal aid and legal services according to the needs of victims;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from victims of violence according to regional financial capacity; and
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children victims of violence.
(3) The obligations of the Village Government as referred to in Article 5 letter a include:
a. establishing policies for the protection of women and children victims of violence, such as Village Regulations on the Protection of Women and Children or Village Head Regulations;
b. incorporating women and child protection programs in the Village Medium-Term Development Plan;
c. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children in the Village Revenue and Expenditure Budget;
d. establishing village posts for integrated services for women and children victims of violence;
e. providing service programs for women and children victims of violence in the village;
f. appointing management and victim assistance officers for village posts;
g. conducting prevention activities in the village;
h. conducting coordination and cooperation with related parties including the community, community-based services and the business sector;
i. conducting guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children at the village level.
(4) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in a regional action plan as a basis for Regional Apparatus Organizations in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(5) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (4) is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).

text:
Pasal 7

(1) Kewajiban dan tanggungjawab masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf b, diselenggarakan dalam bentuk peran serta masyarakat.

(2) Bentuk peran serta masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) meliputi:

a. mencegah terjadinya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. memberikan informasi dan/atau melaporkan tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak kepada penegak hukum atau pihak yang berwenang;
c. turut serta dalam penanganan korban tindak kekerasan;
d. memberikan perlindungan terhadap korban;
e. memberikan pertolongan darurat.

translated_text:
Article 7

(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in Article 5 letter b, are carried out in the form of community participation.

(2) Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. preventing acts of violence against women and children;
b. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties;
c. participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence;
d. providing protection to victims;
e. providing emergency assistance.

text:
Pasal 9

(1) Pencegahan dimaksudkan untuk mengurangi potensi resiko dan kerentanan perempuan dan anak dari segala bentuk kekerasan baik yang terjadi dalam ranah rumah tangga maupun publik, termasuk mencegah keberulangan kekerasan yang dialami korban.

(2) Pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak meliputi:

a. pencegahan kekerasan di lingkungan keluarga dan masyarakat termasuk desa;
b. pencegahan kekerasan di lingkungan pendidikan;
c. pencegahan kekerasan di lingkungan tempat kerja; dan
d. pencegahan kekerasan di transportasi umum
(3) Pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) dapat dilakukan dalam bentuk:
a. sosialisasi terutama kepada kelompok-kelompok yang rentan;
d. membentuk posko desa untuk pelayanan terpadu bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
e. menyediakan program layanan bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan di desa;
f. mengangkat pengurus dan petugas pendamping korban untuk posko desa;
g. melakukan kegiatan pencegahan di desa;
h. melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama dengan pihak terkait termasuk dengan masyarakat, layanan berbasis komunitas dan dunia usaha;
i. melakukan pembinaan dan pengawasan penyelenggaraan perlindungan perempuan dan anak di tingkat desa.
(4) Dalam rangka melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggungjawab sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Bupati menetapkan program dan kegiatan aksi perlindungan perempuan dan anak dalam satu rencana aksi daerah sebagai dasar bagi OPD dalam melaksanakan perlindungan perempuan dan anak dari tindak kekerasan.
(5) Rencana Aksi Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (4) merupakan bagian dari Rencana Pembangunan Jangka Menengah Daerah (RPJMD).

translated_text:
Article 9

(1) Prevention is intended to reduce the potential risk and vulnerability of women and children from all forms of violence that occur both in the domestic and public spheres, including preventing the recurrence of violence experienced by victims.

(2) Prevention of violence against women and children includes:

a. prevention of violence in the family and community environment including villages;
b. prevention of violence in the educational environment;
c. prevention of violence in the workplace environment; and
d. prevention of violence in public transportation
(3) Prevention of violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (2) may be carried out in the form of:
a. socialization especially to vulnerable groups;
d. establishing village posts for integrated services for women and children victims of violence;
e. providing service programs for women and children victims of violence in the village;
f. appointing management and victim assistance officers for village posts;
g. conducting prevention activities in the village;
h. conducting coordination and cooperation with related parties including the community, community-based services and the business sector;
i. conducting guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children at the village level.
(4) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in a regional action plan as a basis for Regional Apparatus Organizations in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(5) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (4) is part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD).

