e. providing emergency assistance.

text:
Bagian Kesatu Bentuk Pelayanan

Pasal 10

(1) Bentuk pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan meliputi:

a. layanan pengaduan;
b. layanan medis;
c. layanan psikologis;
d. layanan rehabilitasi sosial;
e. layanan penegakan dan bantuan hukum;
f. layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial; dan
g. layanan pendampingan;

translated_text:
Part One Forms of Services

Article 10

(1) Forms of services for women and children victims of violence include:

a. complaint services;
b. medical services;
c. psychological services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. law enforcement and legal aid services;
f. repatriation and social reintegration services; and
g. assistance services;

text:
Pasal 11

(1) Layanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 10 huruf a, meliputi ;

a. layanan pemberian informasi mengenai hak-hak dan layanan yang disediakan kepada korban;

b. layanan telpon pengaduan bebas pulsa;

c. layanan penjangkauan; dan

d. layanan konsultasi.

(2) Layanan pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menjadi tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

translated_text:
Article 11

(1) Complaint services as referred to in Article 10 letter a, include;

a. information provision services regarding rights and services provided to victims;

b. toll-free complaint telephone services;

c. outreach services; and

d. consultation services.

(2) Complaint services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of Regional Apparatus Organizations handling women's empowerment and child protection affairs.

text:
Pasal 12

(1) Layanan medis sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 10 huruf b, meliputi ;

a. layanan konsultasi;

b. layanan kegawat daruratan;

c. layanan pemeriksaan;

d. layanan pengobatan dan perawatan, baik rawat jalan maupun rawat inap;

e. layanan rujukan; dan

f. layanan medis yang terkait hukum seperti visum dan tes DNA.

(2) Layanan medis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan melalui;

a. mekanisme khusus di instalansi gawat darurat;

b. petugas medis khusus yang telah dilatih mengenai pelayanan medis untuk perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;

c. koordinasi dengan Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu, Organisasi Perangkat Daerah, aparat penegak hukum, lembaga pendamping korban dan pihak lainnya yang terkait.

(3) Layanan medis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menjadi tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan kesehatan.

(4) Biaya layanan medis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan tanggungjawab Pemerintah Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 12

(1) Medical services as referred to in Article 10 letter b, include;

a. consultation services;

b. emergency services;

c. examination services;

d. treatment and care services, both outpatient and inpatient;

e. referral services; and

f. legal-related medical services such as visum et repertum and DNA tests.

(2) Medical services as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out through;

a. special mechanisms in emergency installations;

b. special medical officers who have been trained in medical services for women and children victims of violence;

c. coordination with Integrated Service Centers, Regional Apparatus Organizations, law enforcement officials, victim assistance institutions and other related parties.

(3) Medical services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of Regional Apparatus Organizations handling health affairs.

(4) Costs of medical services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of the Regional Government.

text:
Pasal 13

(1) Layanan psikologis sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 10 huruf c, meliputi;

a. layanan konseling;

b. layanan pemeriksaan psikologis;

c. layanan psikologis klinis; dan

d. layanan psikiatet.

(2) Layanan psikologis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan oleh petugas khusus yang telah dilatih.

(3) Layanan psikologis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menjadi tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan kesehatan dan urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak dan dapat bekerjasama dengan organisasi profesi dan pihak lainnya yang terkait.

translated_text:
Article 13

(1) Psychological services as referred to in Article 10 letter c, include;

a. counseling services;

b. psychological examination services;

c. clinical psychological services; and

d. psychiatric services.

(2) Psychological services as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by special officers who have been trained.

(3) Psychological services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of Regional Apparatus Organizations handling health affairs and women's empowerment and child protection affairs and may cooperate with professional organizations and other related parties.

text:
Pasal 14

(1) Layanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 10 huruf d, meliputi ;

a. layanan shelter atau rumah aman;

b. layanan pendampingan oleh pekerja sosial;

c. layanan peer group; dan

d. layanan penguatan keluarga korban.

(2) Layanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan oleh petugas khusus yang telah dilatih.

(3) Layanan rehabilitasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) menjadi tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan sosial.

translated_text:
Article 14

(1) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 10 letter d, include;

a. shelter or safe house services;

b. assistance services by social workers;

c. peer group services; and

d. victim family strengthening services.

(2) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by special officers who have been trained.

(3) Social rehabilitation services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of Regional Apparatus Organizations handling social affairs.

text:
Pasal 15

(1) Layanan penegakan dan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 10 huruf e, meliputi

a. lavanan konsultasi hukum:

b. pendampingan oleh kuasa hukum;
c. perlindungan sementara dari pihak kepolisian terhadap ancaman ancaman dan balas dendam yang dialami oleh korban;
d. perlindungan rumah aman dari Lembaga Perlindugan Saksi Korban dan/atau Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu;
e. pendampingan disetiap proses hukum dari lembaga pendamping korban dan/atau dari keluarga; dan
f. pendampingan ahli bahasa atau penerjemah termasuk bahasa isyarat;
(2) Layanan penegakan dan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilakukan oleh petugas yang telah dilatih.
(3) Layanan penegakan dan bantuan hukum sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan hukum dan yang membidangi urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak yang dalam pelaksanaanya dapat bekerjasama dengan lembaga profesi advokat, organisasi bantuan hukum, lembaga pendamping korban, lembaga penegak hukum, Kantor Wilayah Hukum dan HAM serta pihak lainnya yang terkait.

translated_text:
Article 15

(1) Law enforcement and legal aid services as referred to in Article 10 letter e, include

a. legal consultation services:

b. assistance by legal counsel;
c. temporary protection from the police against threats and retaliation experienced by victims;
d. safe house protection from the Witness and Victim Protection Agency and/or Integrated Service Center;
e. assistance in every legal process from victim assistance institutions and/or from family; and
f. assistance of linguists or interpreters including sign language;
(2) Law enforcement and legal aid services as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by officers who have been trained.
(3) Law enforcement and legal aid services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of Regional Apparatus Organizations handling legal affairs and those handling women's empowerment and child protection affairs which in their implementation may cooperate with advocate professional institutions, legal aid organizations, victim assistance institutions, law enforcement agencies, Regional Office of Law and Human Rights as well as other related parties.

text:
Pasal 16

(1) Layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 10 huruf f meliputi :

a. layanan pemulangan dan/atau penjemputan;
b. layanan dokumen kependudukan seperti akte kelahiran, kartu tanda penduduk dan kartu keluarga;
c. lavanan pengasuhan;
d. lavanan pemberian beasiswa sekolah;
e. layanan peningkatan keterampilan dan pemberdayaan ekonomi;
f. layanan penguatan dan/atau konseling keluarga;
g. layanan penguatan dan/atau konseling masyarakat atau penyelenggara lembaga pendidikan; dan
h. layanan pemberian program perlindungan sosial di bidang pendidikan, kesehatan, ekonomi, sosial dan perumahan.
(2) Layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan sosial, urusan pendidikan, urusan kesehatan, urusan pemukiman dan pekerjaan umum, urusan ketenagakerjaan dan urusan koperasi dan UKM, urusan pemberdayaan masyarakat dan desa, urusan perdagangan dan perindustrian, dan urusan kependudukan.
(3) Pelaksanaan layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat bekerjasama dengan dunia usaha, badan zakat, organisasi masyarakat, lembaga swadaya masyarakat dan pihak-pihak lainya yang terkait.

translated_text:
Article 16

(1) Repatriation and social reintegration services as referred to in article 10 letter f include:

a. repatriation and/or pick-up services;
b. population document services such as birth certificates, identity cards and family cards;
c. parenting services;
d. school scholarship provision services;
e. skills enhancement and economic empowerment services;
f. family strengthening and/or counseling services;
g. community strengthening and/or counseling services or educational institution organizers; and
h. social protection program provision services in the fields of education, health, economy, social and housing.
(2) Repatriation and social reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of Regional Apparatus Organizations handling social affairs, education affairs, health affairs, settlement and public works affairs, employment affairs and cooperatives and SMEs affairs, community and village empowerment affairs, trade and industry affairs, and population affairs.
(3) Implementation of repatriation and reintegration services as referred to in paragraph (1) may cooperate with the business community, zakat agencies, community organizations, non-governmental organizations and other related parties.

text:
Pasal 17

(1) Layanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam pasal 10 huruf g meliputi :

a. layanan pendampingan di rumah sakit atau lembaga layanan medis lainnya;
b. layanan pendampingan di lembaga penegak hukum;
c. layanan pendampingan di lembaga-lembaga pemerintah dan lembaga sosial;
d. layanan peer group.
(2) Layanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) merupakan tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.
(3) Pelaksanaan layanan pendampingan dapat dilakukan dengan bekerjasama dengan organisasi sosial, lembaga swadaya masyarakat, lembaga pendamping korban dan perguruan tinggi.

translated_text:
Article 17

(1) Accompaniment services as referred to in article 10 letter g include:

a. accompaniment services in hospitals or other medical service institutions;
b. accompaniment services in law enforcement agencies;
c. accompaniment services in government institutions and social institutions;
d. peer group services.
(2) Accompaniment services as referred to in paragraph (1) are the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus Organization which handles the affairs of women's empowerment and child protection.
(3) Implementation of accompaniment services can be carried out in cooperation with social organizations, non-governmental organizations, victim support institutions and higher education institutions.

Part Two Principles and Service Standards

Article 19

(1) Services for women and children victims of violence as referred to in Article 10 are carried out comprehensively and in an integrated manner across sectors, professions, and academic disciplines.

(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) are organized with the principles of:

a. non-discrimination;
b. equality;
c. protection and confidentiality;
d. honesty;
e. empowerment; and
f. integration.
(3) Services for women and children victims of violence are carried out based on service standards in accordance with laws and regulations.
(4) Service mechanisms for women and children victims of violence are organized according to standard operating procedures.
(5) Standard operating procedures as referred to in paragraph (4) are further regulated by Regent Regulation.

text:
Pasal 21

(1) Pelayanan terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) ditingkat kabupaten dilakukan oleh Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu Kabupaten.

(2) Pembentukan dan fasilitasi penyelenggaraan Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA)ditingkat kabupaten menjadi tanggungjawab Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

(3) Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dibentuk dengan tugas:

a. memberikan layanan korban secara terpadu dan komprehensif;
b. menyediakan layanan pengaduan yang terintegrasi dengan layanan pendampingan, medis dan hukum;
c. melakukan rujukan penanganan kasus sesuai dengan layanan yang dibutuhkan korban;
d. melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama penanganan kasus dengan pihak yang terkait;
e. melakukan pendataan penanganan kasus;
f. menyediakan berbagai informasi yang dibutuhkan korban dan masyarakat;
g. melakukan pencegahan kasus kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak.
(4) Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) terdiri dari;
a. organisasi perangkat daerah yang terkait;
b. rumah sakit pemerintah dan/atau swasta;
c. kepolisian;
d. kejaksaan negeri;
e. pengadilan negeri;
f. advokat;
g. organisasi keagamaan;
h. organisasi masyarakat;
i. organisasi profesi;
j. pemberdayaan dan kesejahteraan keluarga;
k. lembaga pendamping korban; dan
l. lembaga swadaya masyarakat.
(5) Struktur Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) terdiri dari:
a. penasehat;
b. ketua;
c. sekretaris;
d. sekretariat pelayanan;
e. divisi-divisi.
(6) Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) ditetapkan melalui keputusan bupati.

translated_text:
Article 21

(1) Integrated service for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) at the regency level is carried out by the Regency Integrated Service Center.

(2) The establishment and facilitation of the implementation of the Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) at the regency level is the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus Organization which handles the affairs of women's empowerment and child protection.

(3) The Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) is established with the tasks of:

a. providing victim services in an integrated and comprehensive manner;
b. providing complaint services integrated with accompaniment, medical and legal services;
c. making case handling referrals according to the services needed by victims;
d. conducting coordination and cooperation in case handling with related parties;
e. conducting data collection on case handling;
f. providing various information needed by victims and the community;
g. conducting prevention of violence cases against women and children.
(4) The Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. related regional apparatus organizations;
b. government and/or private hospitals;
c. police;
d. district prosecutor's office;
e. district court;
f. advocates;
g. religious organizations;
h. community organizations;
i. professional organizations;
j. family empowerment and welfare;
k. victim support institutions; and
l. non-governmental organizations.
(5) The structure of the Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. advisor;
b. chairperson;
c. secretary;
d. service secretariat;
e. divisions.
(6) The Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) is established through a regent's decree.

text:
Pasal 22

(1) Pelayanan terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) ditingkat kecamatan dilakukan oleh Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu Kecamatan.

(2) Pembentukan dan fasilitasi penyelenggaraan Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) ditingkat kecamatan menjadi tanggungjawabOrganisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak dan bagian tata pemerintahan.

(3) Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dibentuk dengan tugas:

a. memberikan layanan korban secara terpadu dan komprehensif di tingkat kecamatan;
b. menyediakan layanan pengaduan;
c. melakukan rujukan penanganan kasus sesuai dengan layanan yang dibutuhkan korban kepada Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu Kabupaten dan pihak terkait di tingkat kecamatan;
d. melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama penanganan kasus dengan pihak terkait di tingkat kecamatan;
e. melakukan pendataan penanganan kasus di tingkat kecamatan;
f. menyediakan berbagai informasi yang dibutuhkan korban dan masyarakat di tingkat kecamatan;
g. melakukan pencegahan kasus kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak di tingkat kecamatan.
(4) Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PPTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) terdiri dari:
a. pemerintah kecamatan;
b. unit pelaksana teknis dinas di kecamatan;
c. kepolisian sektor;
d. puskesmas;
e. pemberdayaan dan kesejahteraan keluarga;
f. organisasi masyarakat;
g. organisasi keagamaan. (5) Struktur Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) terdiri dari : a. penasehat; b. ketua; c. sekretaris; d. sekretariat pelayanan; e. divisi divisi. (6) Struktur Pusat Pelayanan Terpadu perlindungan perempuan dan anak (PTPPA) sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (5) ditetapkan melalui keputusan kepala Organisasi Perangkat Daerah yang membidangi urusan pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak.

translated_text:
Article 22

(1) Integrated service for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) at the sub-district level is carried out by the Sub-District Integrated Service Center.

(2) The establishment and facilitation of the implementation of the Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) at the sub-district level is the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus Organization which handles the affairs of women's empowerment and child protection and the government administration section.

(3) The Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) is established with the tasks of:

a. providing victim services in an integrated and comprehensive manner at the sub-district level;
b. providing complaint services;
c. making case handling referrals according to the services needed by victims to the Regency Integrated Service Center and related parties at the sub-district level;
d. conducting coordination and cooperation in case handling with related parties at the sub-district level;
e. conducting data collection on case handling at the sub-district level;
f. providing various information needed by victims and the community at the sub-district level;
g. conducting prevention of violence cases against women and children at the sub-district level.
(4) The Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PPTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. sub-district government;
b. technical implementation unit of the agency in the sub-district;
c. sector police;
d. community health center;
e. family empowerment and welfare;
f. community organizations;
g. religious organizations. (5) The structure of the Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of: a. advisor; b. chairperson; c. secretary; d. service secretariat; e. divisions. (6) The structure of the Integrated Service Center for the protection of women and children (PTPPA) as referred to in paragraph (5) is established through a decree of the head of the Regional Apparatus Organization which handles the affairs of women's empowerment and child protection.
